# Deferred: read-only detail Share → social messaging

**Status:** Parked until **in-app social messaging / share-to-friend** is wired. Do not re-enable in shipping UI unless the user asks.

## Why parked

`ReadOnlyItemDetailView` and `ReadOnlyOutfitDetailView` showed a share control via `SocialEngagementActionsRow` gated on `appCapabilities.enablesFriendsAndSharing`, but `onShare` was a no-op. Real share depends on messaging (send item/outfit to a friend), not system share sheet alone.

Own-content `ItemDetailView` / `OutfitDetailView` share flows are separate and may already use friends sheets — leave those alone unless asked.

## Current baseline

Both read-only detail views pass `showsShareButton: false` (with a code comment pointing here).

## When revisiting

1. Wire `onShare` to the social messaging / share-to-friend flow for the remote item or outfit.
2. Re-enable with something like `showsShareButton: appCapabilities.enablesFriendsAndSharing` (or a dedicated messaging capability if one is added).
3. Remove the deferred comments / this rule once shipping.
